{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>ואלה</b> notarikon: וחייב אדם לחקור הדין (a person is obligated to investigate the law). המשפטים — notarikon: הדיין מצווה שיעשה פשרה טרם יעשה משפט (the judge is commanded to make a compromise before rendering judgment). אשר — notarikon: אם שניהם רוצין (if both of them want)." "<b>ואלה המשפטים אשר תשים</b> ס\"ת מרמה — if a fraudulent case comes before the judge, he shall investigate and inquire to bring it to its truth." "<b>המשפטים אשר</b> mem: 40 laws. And the word אשר — notarikon: אלו מנעל שופר רצועה." "<b>אשר תשים לפניהם</b> in gematria: דקדוקי התורה ודקדוקי סופרים. And there are five words in the verse, to teach you that whoever judges a true judgment to its truth — as if he fulfilled the five books of the Torah, and as if he became a partner to HaShem blessed be He in the act of Creation."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:51.003081937Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}